        "text": "Money is simply a tool to exchange value. It is accepted as payment because everyone shares the belief that it has value. In this sense, what we actually use as a unit of account for money is less relevant. Basically, any object could be used as money in some cultures. Even rocks and seashells were used as money in the past. Today, inmates may use cigarettes or coffee as money in prisons. Money has value because our society believes it has value. Of course, some objects are more suitable for this than others. For example, gold was used as money before the creation of paper money. It worked well because it's scarce and durable, but it's also heavy and it can be difficult to transport and divide, so it became inconvenient for everyday use.",
        "start": 240,
        "end": 46120,
        "confidence": 0.9811772,
